# YourWalk

City of Casey pilot. Phase B pipeline + scoring complete (Accepted v1.1 / v1.1.2). Phase C (from 15 Jul 2026) = PostGIS load + Next.js/Mapbox app build.

CrowdLab-wide conventions are injected every session from `~/.cursor/crowdlab/conventions.md`. This file is YourWalk-specific only.

## Product name

- **YourWalk** — one word, PascalCase in all prose, UI, docs, filenames, and commit messages.
- **Not** "Your Walk", "your walk", or `your_walk` (except the repo directory name `yourwalk/`).
- Package/module prefixes may use `yourwalk_` (e.g. `yourwalk_pipeline/`).

## Methodology gate

Before ingestion or scoring code, read `docs/VULNERABILITY_INDEX.md` **v1.1** (not v0.2).

Locked model:
- Day Index = Accessibility 60% + Heat/Shade 40%
- Night Index = Accessibility 60% + Lighting/After Dark 40%
- Speed zones and graffiti → shared Accessibility 60%
- Fountains + benches → Day Index (Heat & Shade stream)
- Toilets, dog bags, YourGround → overlays only, not in index
- Segment network = Footpaths T1EAM (~27k segments)

Pending Council data (crossings, kerb ramps): reduced confidence until received; never impute missing as zero.

## Pipeline

- Scripts live in `pipeline/scripts/`
- Shared helpers in `pipeline/yourwalk_pipeline/`
- Raw and intermediate data under `pipeline/data/` (gitignored)
- Document downloads in `pipeline/README.md`
- One ingestion script per dataset; include QA step before GeoParquet export
- Workshop stack (not production): DuckDB + GeoParquet → PostGIS per CrowdLab playbook analytical tooling

