## Documentation

- Repo is source of truth; link Notion to repo paths, do not duplicate methodology
- `docs/PRD.md` is product source of truth — do not invent requirements; use Open Questions with options + decision criteria when unclear
- Update `docs/DECISIONS.md` for architecture changes (ADR format)
- Given/When/Then acceptance criteria for requirements; backlog items trace to PRD
- Prefer vertical slices (end-to-end user value) over component-only work
- CEO-readable PRD; push technical detail into companion docs

## Privacy and language

- Anonymous by default (ADR-004 leaning)
- Never imply safety guarantees or crime prediction
- Graffiti is environmental order proxy, not crime data
- Minimise sensitive data; transparency on provenance and confidence in UI (when UI exists)
- WCAG 2.1 AA when building UI; performance budgets per `docs/PHASES.md`

## Pilot context

- Casey first; scalable to other LGAs without over-engineering multi-tenancy in MVP
- Documentation should support grant reporting; see `docs/COMMS_AND_ENGAGEMENT.md`
